  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000121097,
      "SummaryText": "This EPA RMP was prepared in accordance with the requirements of the Clean Air Act \u00a7 112(r), OSHA 29 CFR \u00a7 1910.119, and U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) at 40 CFR \u00a768. The OSHA PSM and EPA Subpart D RMP standards are applicable to operations at this Plant.  The electronic RMP summarizes the policies and procedures implemented by the Plant to minimize the likelihood of an accident. The electronic RMP also summarizes the actions that the Plant has taken to ensure that a response to a release will be implemented in a proper and timely manner.\nPURPOSE FOR UPDATING RMP\nHelena Industries, LLC (Helena) is resubmitting the EPA RMP to add covered processes for the storage and handling of Isopropylamine (75-31-0).  Also, corrections to off-site consequence analyses for   All accident prevention elements have been reviewed and/or updated. \nFACILITY\nThe operations at this Plant consist of agricultural and turf and ornamental chemical storage and handling, blending, and distribution.  Compliance with federal and state regulations is a priority.  The following company programs are in place in addition to the EPA Risk Management Program (RMP) and OSHA Process Safety Management (PSM): Spill Prevention Control and Countermeasures (SPCC) Plan, Hazard Communication, Community Right-To-Know, Safety Committee, National Pollutant Discharge Elimination System (NPDES) Permit for stormwater management, and HAZWOPER.  \nWith respect to the EPA RMP and OSHA PSM, the regulated substances and associated covered processes at this Plant are as follows: \nAqua ammonia (24.3% ammonia concentration) is stored and handled at quantities that exceed the regulatory threshold quantity.  Aqua ammonia covered processes operated at this Plant include:\no Covered Process 1: Aqua Ammonia Storage & Handling  \no Covered Process 2: Plant Micronutrient Formulation with Aqua Ammonia  \nDimethylamine is stored and handled in an aqueous solution (60% dimethylamine concentration) at quantities that exceed the"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000121097,
      "SummaryText": "regulatory threshold quantity.  Dimethylamine covered processes operated at this Plant include:\no Covered Process 3: Dimethylamine Storage  \no Covered Process 4: Dimethylamine Processing\nIsopropylamine is stored and handled at quantities that exceed the regulatory threshold quantity.  Isopropylamine covered processes operated at this Plant include:\no Covered Process 5: Isopropylamine Storage  \no Covered Process 6: Isopropylamine Processing\n\n\nACCIDENT PREVENTION PROGRAM\nThe Safety Health & Environmental (SHE) Manager implements the risk management planning (and process safety management) process at this Plant. The SHE Manager is assisted by other trained personnel as directed. The SHE Manager is responsible for ensuring that its employees are properly trained in the implementation of the Program 2 and 3 Accident Prevention Program elements as related to their responsibilities.  The accident prevention program elements addressed in the PSM/RMP combined program includes: Management System, Employee Participation, Process Safety Information, Process Hazard Analysis, Operating Procedures, Training, Contractor, Pre-Startup Review, Mechanical Integrity, Hot Work Permit, Management of Change, Incident Investigation, Emergency Response, Compliance Audits, and Trade Secrets.\nThe SHE Manager is also responsible for maintaining and implementing the site\u0092s Spill Prevention Control and Countermeasures (SPCC) Plan.  This plan outlines procedures for Plant operations pertaining to oil products, and by extension, all other liquid chemical products handled at the Plant.  \nEMERGENCY RESPONSE PROGRAM\nThis is a non-responding facility. The Plant has coordinated emergency response activities with its local emergency response agency and local fire department.  \nThe Plant will clean up incidental spills of chemical products.  Employees are trained annually on the emergency action plan, including completion of emergency evacuation drills. \nFIVE YEAR ACCIDENT HISTORY\nThere have been no on-si"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 2,
      "FacilityID": 1000121097,
      "SummaryText": "te deaths, injuries, or significant property damage; or off-site deaths, injuries, property damage, evacuations, or sheltering in place, in the past five (5) years because of the operations involving regulated chemicals at this Plant.\nPLANNED CHANGES TO IMPROVE SAFETY\nThe Plant will address each recommendation listed in the process hazard analysis (PHA). In summary, the PHA recommendations include, but are not limited to:\n\u0095\tUpdate the Plant PSM/RMP program to reflect the EPA RMP rule changes published May 2024"
